============================================================================================================
G08 -- THE FRAMEWORK'S STRUCTURE-FORMATION STORY: how the LSS
       assembled -- the phantom's condensation-first narrative vs CDM's
       growth-first, stated quantitatively
============================================================================================================

  THE COMMITTED SET: m = 5.09 keV (G212); the galaxy well M_b = 7.0e+10 Msun
  with sigma = 119.2 km/s (the triad); a0 = 9.36190e-11 m/s^2; T_0 = 2.72548 K;
  z*(galaxy) = 2.4262 (germ) in the G132 band [2.3656, 2.4932];
  M_sat = 3.09e+14 Msun (G140/G178); the pie @ R500 (G179): baryons 17.7% /
  phantom 56.9% / dust 24.6%; dust share of Omega_dm = 0.9921 (G079).

============================================================================================================
PART 1  THE TWO NARRATIVES, STATED QUANTITATIVELY
============================================================================================================

  1a  CDM -- DARK-FIRST (growth-first): the sigma_8-normalized hierarchy
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------
      P(k) = A k^0.9649 T^2(k) (EH98 full CDM+baryon transfer), normalized to
      sigma_8 = 0.811.  sigma(M) FALLS with mass, so the collapse hierarchy
      builds from the BOTTOM: the first bound structures are the smallest.
  THE FIRST-COLLAPSE MAP (this pipeline, UNVERIFIED; the transfer grid
  truncates at k = 300 h/Mpc, so the deep-end z_coll is a LOWER bound --
  the deciding observable decade k ~ 100-500 h/Mpc sits ABOVE the truncation):
      M [Msun]   sigma(M,0)     z_coll                                   
       1.0e-01        9.468        6.1                                   
       1.0e+02        9.461        6.1                                   
       1.0e+04        9.320        6.0                                   
       1.0e+06        7.817        4.9                                   
       1.0e+08        5.577        3.2                                   
       1.0e+10        3.602        1.7                                   
       1.0e+12        1.994        0.3                                   
       1.0e+13        1.361        ---                                   
      -- the deep-end sigma saturates at ~9.5 (the 300 h/Mpc truncation),
         so this pipeline's z_coll ~ 6-8 is a FLOOR; the literature CDM
         microhalos (M ~ 1e-6-1e3 Msun, WIMP free-streaming; Green+05, 
         Diemand+05, Angulo+17) form at z ~ 30-60 [UNVERIFIED citations]:
         THE FIRST OBJECTS ARE DARK.
      -- the baryons do NOT follow at that scale: the baryon filtering/
         Jeans scale M_J ~ 1e4-1e5 Msun means the microhalos stay BARYON-
         EMPTY (the first stars need atomic cooling, M ~ 1e7-1e8, z ~ 20-30)
         [UNVERIFIED literature].  Dark well first, baryons later -- every
         observed halo.
      -- the well's dark/baryon ratio is the COSMIC one: Omega_dm/Omega_b
         = 5.355 (the baryons fall in at the cosmic fraction f_b = 0.1564).
  [PASS] G1 [CDM input spectrum] sigma_8 = 0.811 reproduced exactly; the growth factor g(z) (CPT92): g(0.5), g(1), g(2.4) = 0.77, 0.61, 0.37
         measured: sigma(8 h^-1 Mpc) = 0.8110; g(0.5) = 0.770, g(1) = 0.608, g(2.43) = 0.367
         reading : the growth factor halves between z = 0 and z ~ 1.5 and is 0.37 at the framework's z* = 2.4: after z* only 37% of today's linear amplitude was present -- CDM's cluster-scale assembly (sigma(3e14) = 0.66 today) is dominated by z < 1 growth (nu(3.09e14, z* = 2.4) = 7.0).

  1b  THE FRAMEWORK -- BARYON-FIRST (condensation-first)
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------
      THE BARYONIC SKELETON comes first: the visible matter's OWN evolution
      (the SFRD rises from z ~ 8 to its z ~ 2 peak; the JWST record shows
      galaxies at z ~ 10-13 [UNVERIFIED citations: Donnan+23, Boylan-Kolchin 23]).
      THE PHANTOM CONDENSES SECOND, when the equilibrium allows:
        T_b(5.09, 119.2) = 9.3380 K  ->  z* = 2.4262 (the G132 band [2.3656,
        2.4932]): the galaxy-class phantom consolidated at COSMIC NOON.
        NO PHANTOM BEFORE z*: for z > z* the CMB thermostat is HOTTER than
        the equilibrium (T_CMB(13) = 38.2 K, T_CMB(4) = 13.6 K > T_b = 9.338
        K): the equilibrium does not exist; the sector is the free dust,
        and there is no phantom gas waiting to condense (the occupation at
        decoupling is e^-6.44e6 = 10^-2.80e6 -- EMPTY, D06 C2).
