  2b  THE PHANTOM'S DRESSING: the phantom + dust complete the halo
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------
  THE STATE TODAY (G179, the 12 X-COP clusters, closure SUM/M500 = 1 EXACT):
    at R500: baryons 17.7% (the skeleton) + phantom 56.9% (the dressing)
    + dust 24.6% (the completion) = 100.0%  (M_dyn = M_b + M_ph + M_dust)
    the phantom's share 56.9% at R500 IS the equipartition identity
    extended: M_ph(<r) = M_b r/r_M; the dust (24.6% at R500; f_dark = 6-10
    in M200) is the remainder.
  THE DUST'S ROLE IN THE FORMATION: the dust is the COLLISIONLESS component
  (G103: relaxes never, t_relax ~ 1e73-1e76 t_H) that carries ~99% of the
  cosmic dark budget (G079: dust share 0.9921; Omega_eq = 0.0021 = 0.79% of
  Omega_dm, uncapped 1.28%%).  Its structure: the measured envelope
  c_dust = 0.72 (M500/8e14)^-0.414 (r/R500)^-0.99 (G143) -- it DRESSES the
  baryonic skeleton from the well outward; its scale is the warm 5.09-keV
  one: lambda_fs = 0.5584 Mpc, k_hm = 57.22 h/Mpc, M_hm ~ 7.34e+05-8.41e+06 Msun
  (S07/G115): the dust CANNOT clump below the sub-halo decade -- there the
  phantom's charge face (R(k) = 1) rides on top (S07's composite)
  R_comp(k) = (1-f_d) + f_d T^2(k; 5.09).

  THE COMPOSITE ASSEMBLY TIMELINE (the state, per class):
    PRE-z*  : the baryonic skeleton assembles (galaxies present z > z*;
              T_CMB(13) = 38.2 K > T_b = 9.34 K: the JWST-era galaxies had
