============================================================================================================
PART 3  THE OBSERVABLE DISCRIMINATOR: where the two stories differ
============================================================================================================

  3a  THE FIRST OBJECTS: CDM microhalos vs the framework's baryonic galaxies
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------
    CDM (growth-first): the first bound structures are DARK -- WIMP
    microhalos M ~ 1e-6-1e3 Msun at z ~ 30-60 [UNVERIFIED literature:
    Green+05, Diemand+05, Angulo+17]; baryon-empty below the ~1e4-1e5
    filtering scale; the first STARS need atomic cooling (M ~ 1e7-1e8).
    THE FRAMEWORK (baryon-first): no dark object smaller than a baryonic
    well exists -- (i) the phantom has NO mass below the baryonic skeleton
    (the freeze floor sigma_min = 65 km/s @ 5 keV -> z* = 0.019; the dSph
    class NEVER condensed, z* < 0, D06); (ii) the dust cannot clump below
    M_hm ~ 7.34e+05 Msun (lambda_fs = 0.558 Mpc, the warm cut).  FIRST OBJECTS
    = THE FIRST BARYONIC GALAXIES.
    THE OBSERVED FIRST-OBJECT RECORD: JWST's z ~ 10-13 galaxies as the
    baryon-first signature -- the UV luminosity function at z ~ 9-13
    EXCEEDS the pre-JWST CDM-based extrapolations, and the most massive
    early candidates sit above the CDM halo mass function's supply of
    halos bright enough ('too many early galaxies' -- UNVERIFIED citations:
    Donnan+23 MNRAS 518, 6011; Boylan-Kolchin 23 NatAst 7, 731): a lean
    toward baryon-first at the FIRST-OBJECT level, still UNVERIFIED.
    THE REGISTERED HIGH-z TEST (the framework's own): galaxies at z > z*
    have NO phantom (T_CMB > T_b = 9.34 K): their internal dynamics should
    show the BARYONIC FLOOR sigma_b = (G M_b a0)^(1/4)/sqrt(2) -- e.g.
    sigma_b(7e10) = 121.4 km/s -- instead of the dark-filled CDM
    expectation at the same stellar mass.  A z > 2.4 sample of resolved
    galaxy dispersions discriminates: dispersions at the baryonic floor =
    baryon-first; dispersions carrying the 5.35:1 dark ratio = dark-first.
  [PASS] G10 [first objects] the framework's first-object floor: the phantom has no mass below the baryonic well (freeze floor z*(65 km/s) = 0.019 ~ 0; dSph z* < 0) and the dust cuts at M_hm ~ 7.34e+05 Msun; the observed first objects ARE galaxies (JWST z ~ 10-13, UNVERIFIED)
         measured: z*(65) = 0.019; M_hm = 7.34e+05; JDWS first record at z ~ 10-13
         reading : CDM's first objects are dark microhalos (below every baryonic scale, UNVERIFIED literature); the framework's are the baryonic galaxies -- the first-object record (JWST, UNVERIFIED excess) and the z > z* dynamics floor are the registered discriminators.

  3b  THE 21-CM EVOLUTION (the G05/G115 lane): the EoR power at k ~ 30-100
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------
    The free-streaming damping tail of the warm dust lives in the EoR
    21-cm statistics (G115 D2/V3: the floor's signature is '21-cm/epoch-of-
    reionization and small-scale lensing', not the resolved forest).
    THE COMPOSITE 21-cm POWER RATIO  R_comp(k) = (1-f_d) + f_d T^2(k; 5.09):
      T^2(30) = 0.7075, T^2(100) = 0.0163 (registers 0.7074/0.0162 reproduced);
      f_d = 0.98 (the dust's budget share 99.2%): R_comp(30) = 0.7098,
      R_comp(100) = 0.0240 -- vs the CHARGE face R = 1 EXACT.
    THE DISCRIMINATOR: the EoR 21-cm power spectrum at k ~ 30-100 h/Mpc:
      charge (baryon-first phantom dressing, R = 1): FULL CDM power;
      warm-dust-dominated: (0.710)^2 = 0.504 x the power at k = 30, and
      (0.024)^2 = 0.001 x at k = 100 -- a factor-2 to factor-40 power
      contrast between the two readings of the same sector (a HERA-class, 
      future measurement; the current global-signal probes do not resolve
      k ~ 30-100 -- stated honestly).
  [PASS] G11 [21-cm discriminator] the EoR power at k = 30 differs by a factor (R_comp)^2 = 0.504 between the charge face (R = 1) and the budget-fraction warm dust (f_d = 0.98) -- the 21-cm evolution is a registered discriminator (G115/G05: the damping tail lives in the EoR statistics)
         measured: R_comp(30; 0.98) = 0.7098; power ratio = 0.504; T^2(30/100) = 0.7075/0.0163
         reading : the identical sector reads 'full power' (charge, the phantom's R(k) = 1 dressing) or 'damped' (the warm dust at the budget fraction) at the EoR 21-cm scales -- 0.51x in power at k = 30, 1e-3x at k = 100; the k ~ 100-500 deciding decade (G156) is the same decade, and the 21-cm window is its EoR face.

  3c  THE SUB-HALO CENSUS (G215, the framework's lean) + the pre-registered
